1. `creating a map when int is key and value is pair` : `map <int,pair<int,int> > r`
		1. `Inserting in such map` : `m.insert({a,{b,c}})` because value will be only one but that one will have further 
        parts so 
		    use `{}` braces.
		2. `Accessing values from such map`: suppose c is a iterator for map created and we are in a loop then`c.first` 
        this will
		    give key `c.second.first` this will give first value of value part of the map `c.second.second` this will 
        give second
		    value of value part of a map. 
		    
		    
2. `Sorting keys of a map in descending order`: by d efault keys of a map are sorted in ascending order but to sort 
    them in descending order `map <int,pair<int,int> ,greater<int>> r`.


3. `multimap` : this works almost as it as map works but use when you wanted to use duplicate keys . 
